  "evidences": [
    {
      "id": "ev_1",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "CiscoTalos_SeaTurtle-DNS-hijacking(07-09-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "executive_summary",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s1"
      },
      "text": "After several months of activity, the actors behind the \"Sea Turtle\" DNS hijacking campaign are not slowing down.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_7",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "CiscoTalos_SeaTurtle-DNS-hijacking(07-09-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "executive_summary",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s7"
      },
      "text": "We also identified a new wave of victims, including a country code top-level domain (ccTLD) registry, which manages the DNS records for every domain uses that particular country code, that access was used to then compromise additional government entities.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_9",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "CiscoTalos_SeaTurtle-DNS-hijacking(07-09-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s9"
      },
      "text": "blog.talosintelligence.com /2019/07/sea-turtle-keeps-on-swimming.html",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_10",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "CiscoTalos_SeaTurtle-DNS-hijacking(07-09-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s1"
      },
      "text": "Talos now has moderate confidence that the threat actors behind Sea Turtle have been using another DNS hijacking technique.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_16",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "CiscoTalos_SeaTurtle-DNS-hijacking(07-09-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s7"
      },
      "text": "Whereas previously reported name server domains such as ns1[.]intersecdns[.]com were used to target multiple organizations.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_20",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "CiscoTalos_SeaTurtle-DNS-hijacking(07-09-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s11"
      },
      "text": "Based on Cisco telemetry, we determined that the actors behind the Sea Turtle campaign had access to the ICS-Forth network.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_21",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "CiscoTalos_SeaTurtle-DNS-hijacking(07-09-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s12"
      },
      "text": "Cisco telemetry confirmed that the actors behind Sea Turtle maintained access to the ICS- Forth network from an operational command and control (C2) node.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_22",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "CiscoTalos_SeaTurtle-DNS-hijacking(07-09-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s13"
      },
      "text": "Our telemetry indicates that the actors maintained access in the ICS-Forth network through at least April 24, five days after the statement was publicly released.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_23",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "CiscoTalos_SeaTurtle-DNS-hijacking(07-09-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s14"
      },
      "text": "Upon analysis of this operational C2 node, we determined that it was also used to access an organization in Syria that was previously redirected using the actor-controlled name server ns1[.]intersecdns[.]com.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_26",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "CiscoTalos_SeaTurtle-DNS-hijacking(07-09-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s2"
      },
      "text": "Notably, this particular C2 node searched for both blog.talosintelligence.com and ncsc.gov.uk, presumably to view Talos' previous reports on DNS hijacking and this DNS hijacking advisory from the United Kingdom's National Cyber Security Centre.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_27",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "CiscoTalos_SeaTurtle-DNS-hijacking(07-09-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s3"
      },
      "text": "New actor-controlled nameserver We recently discovered a new actor-controlled nameserver, rootdnservers[.]com, that exhibited similar behavior patterns as name servers previously utilized as part of the Sea Turtle campaign.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_28",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "CiscoTalos_SeaTurtle-DNS-hijacking(07-09-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s4"
      },
      "text": "The domain rootdnservers[.]com was registered on April 5, 2019 through the registrar NameCheap.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_29",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "CiscoTalos_SeaTurtle-DNS-hijacking(07-09-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s5"
      },
      "text": "The new actor-controlled name server rootdnservers[.]com was utilized to perform DNS hijacking against three government entities that all used .gr, the Greek ccTLD.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_30",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "CiscoTalos_SeaTurtle-DNS-hijacking(07-09-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s6"
      },
      "text": "It's likely that these hijackings were performed through the access the threat actors obtained in the ICS-Forth network.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
